nvidia: cold attach to a GPU tzmon powered off at boot; Resizable BAR + BAR restore, verified, in it and in the RTD3 resume

Measured 2026-11-11 on lixi (boot-once BE 48, hardware.graphics.nvidia.rtd3 with tzmon opted out): the thermal guard
read 80 C at its first sample, 5 s after the kernel banner, and rebooted. With tzmon opted out the GPU is powered and
unmanaged from power-on through the loader and the kernel boot. With tzmon on it is cut about 2 s after the banner,
but tzmon offlines every function of the GPU, and devfsadm never attaches an offline node.

The cold attach: the nvidia pseudo node gets a root-only minor, nvidia-poweron. Its open (site/solnix-nvidia, after
the guard is sampling) finds the offline nvidia-bound NVIDIA display node whose root port's _PR3 power resource reads
_STA 0, evaluates _ON, waits for Data Link Layer Link Active, 100 ms and the vendor id, then restores the GPU's BIOS
layout: the GPU has been through a fundamental reset (BARs 0, every Resizable BAR at its default size, Max_Payload_Size
128). With memory and I/O decode off it writes the Resizable BAR control sizes (from the sizes in assigned-addresses,
checked against the capability's supported sizes), then the BAR bases, then Device Control's MPS from the root port.
It then VERIFIES from config space: the vendor/device/subsystem ids against the node's properties, every BAR's base and
size (the standard sizing probe) against assigned-addresses, and each Resizable BAR control's size field. Any mismatch,
or a GPU not in D0: D3hot, _OFF again, every difference logged, and the open fails (EIO); nvidia stays detached and RM
never sees a mis-sized BAR. Otherwise ndi_devi_online attaches nvidia, and RTD3 powers it off 10 s later.

The RTD3 resume (nvidia_rtd3.c) had the same hazard: pci_restore_config_regs() writes the saved 4K image in register
order, so the command register (decode on) and the BARs go back before the Resizable BAR control, after which a BAR is
undefined (PCIe 6.0 7.8.6). BAR1 of the X1E's RTX 3080 Ti is 16 GB (assigned-addresses), a resized BAR. After the
image, the resume now redoes the sizes and bases with decode off, verifies them as above, and only then restores the
command register and D0. On a mismatch it puts the GPU back in D3hot, evaluates _OFF and fails the open.
The attach's sibling offline skips functions tzmon already offlined.
Not redone after the power cycle: the error-reporting enables pcie_initchild set at boot (an offline node keeps
DS_INITIALIZED, so online does not re-run initchild); MRRS and relaxed ordering are at their reset defaults.

